.TH "LINTO-CONFIG" 1

.SH "Configuration"
.PP
The repository's \fBconfig\.yml\fP controls active command groups,
generated command stubs, the Quarto extension default, and Markdown viewer
preferences\.

.SS "Groups and command stubs"
.PP
The \fBgroups\fP mapping accepts the \fBdefault\fP shorthand or a mapping of options:
.RS
.PP
.nf
groups:
  beta: default
  biblo: default
  launch: default
  linto:
    short\-stubs: false
  quarto:
    short\-stubs: false
  utils: default
  old:
    enable: false
  biblio: default
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBdefault\fP enables a group and uses the defaults \fBenable: true\fP and
\fBshort\-stubs: true\fP\. A mapping may set \fBenable: false\fP to leave a directory in
the checkout while making Linto ignore it for dispatch, help, completions, and
stubs\. \fBshort\-stubs: true\fP adds \fBlinto\-COMMAND\fP stubs for command names unique
across enabled groups\. Group\-qualified calls such as \fBlinto GROUP COMMAND\fP and
stubs such as \fBlinto\-GROUP\-COMMAND\fP remain available\.

.SS "Markdown viewer"
.PP
\fBmarkdown\-viewer\fP accepts one command name or an ordered YAML list\. Linto tries
the entries from top to bottom and runs the first installed supported viewer\.
For example:
.RS
.PP
.nf
markdown\-viewer:
  \- mdless
  \- mdcat
  \- glow
  \- bat
  \- cat
.fi
.RE
.PP
Supported choices include \fBmd\-tui\fP, \fBinlyne\fP, \fBmdcat\fP, \fBmandown\fP, \fBglow\fP,
\fBfrogmouth\fP, \fBmdless\fP, \fBmdfried\fP, \fBbat\fP, and \fBcat\fP\. \fBmandown\fP is selected only
when \fBgroff\fP is also installed\. If no configured viewer is available, Linto
falls back to \fBcat\fP\. Set \fBLINTO_MDVIEWER\fP to override the configured list for a
single invocation, for example \fBLINTO_MDVIEWER=cat linto help config\fP\.
.PP
The \fBlinto linto mdsetup\fP command reports the selected viewer and attempts to
install Markdown prerequisites when needed\. It does not install every optional
viewer\.

.SS "Zed data sharing"
.PP
The Zed launcher accepts \fB\-u DIR\fP/\fB\-\-userdatadir DIR\fP; projects using the same
root use the same \fBDIR/\.zed\fP user\-data directory\. Without this option, each
project uses its own \fB\.zed\fP directory\. The launcher initializes a non\-default
\fB\.zed\fP directory once per Linto \fBversion\fP in \fBconfig\.yml\fP: it opens a temporary
Zed window, waits for you to close it, then links \fBlanguages\fP and \fBextensions\fP
to the corresponding directories in \fB$HOME/\.zed\fP\. Other local Zed data,
including project\-specific configuration and themes, is left in place\.

.SS "Refresh generated files"
.PP
After editing configuration or adding/removing executable scripts, run:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto linto refresh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Refresh regenerates command stubs, shell completion data, the active\-group list
in the dispatcher man page, and one man page per \fBlinto\-guide/*\.md\fP topic\. Topic
man pages are installed under \fBman/man1/\fP after generation succeeds and each
page passes \fBgroff \-Wall\fP validation\. \fBmandown\fP and \fBgroff\fP are required for this
step\.
.PP
Register or re\-enable a group with \fBlinto linto addgroup DIRECTORY\fP\. Remove a
group from Linto's active configuration with \fBlinto linto rmgroup GROUP\fP; this
does not delete the group directory\. Use \fBlinto \-\-list\-groups\fP to inspect active
groups\.
